WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.934 --> 00:00:01.768 line:0%
-Our next guest can be seen

00:00:01.768 --> 00:00:03.402 line:0%
on his nationwide stand-up tour,

00:00:03.402 --> 00:00:04.603 line:0%
that includes a night

00:00:04.603 --> 00:00:07.307 line:0%
at the Vivint Arena
in Salt Lake City --

00:00:07.307 --> 00:00:09.175 line:0%
an Arena, oh, my goodness,
how fun --

00:00:09.175 --> 00:00:10.376 line:0%
November 24th.

00:00:10.376 --> 00:00:13.846 line:0%
Please welcome the very funny
Ryan Hamilton!

00:00:13.846 --> 00:00:16.482
[ The Roots playing funk ]
[ Cheering and applause ]

00:00:16.482 --> 00:00:22.588 line:0%
♪♪

00:00:22.588 --> 00:00:25.191
-Thank you.
Thank you.

00:00:25.191 --> 00:00:27.259
Hi. You're not
going to believe this.

00:00:27.259 --> 00:00:28.595
I'm from Idaho.

00:00:28.595 --> 00:00:30.997
[ Cheering and applause ]
Maybe you do believe that.

00:00:30.997 --> 00:00:32.331
[ Laughter ]

00:00:32.331 --> 00:00:33.899
It's strange.

00:00:33.899 --> 00:00:36.368
That's enough to get a laugh
in New York City, really.

00:00:36.368 --> 00:00:39.605
[ Laughter ]
It doesn't really register
here, you know?

00:00:39.605 --> 00:00:41.941
It's just people go, right now,
are looking at me, going,

00:00:41.941 --> 00:00:44.277
"This guy from Iowa
is pretty interesting."

00:00:44.277 --> 00:00:46.445
[ Laughter ]
That's how it is.
I love this city,

00:00:46.445 --> 00:00:49.115
but it's not my default setting,
you know?

00:00:49.115 --> 00:00:51.483
There's a rhythm to this city

00:00:51.483 --> 00:00:54.687
that I have to get into
and I can feel it coming.

00:00:54.687 --> 00:00:57.890
My chest starts to tighten up,
my thoughts start to whirl.

00:00:57.890 --> 00:00:59.859
It's like I'm getting
into double Dutch.

00:00:59.859 --> 00:01:02.061
[ Laughter and applause ]
I can feel it.

00:01:02.061 --> 00:01:04.463
It's like,
"I'm going to New York.

00:01:04.463 --> 00:01:06.065
[ Laughter ]
I'm going to New York.

00:01:06.065 --> 00:01:08.267
I'm in New York.
I'm in New York.

00:01:08.267 --> 00:01:09.769
[ Laughter and applause ]
Don't touch me.

00:01:09.769 --> 00:01:11.137
[ Cheering ]

00:01:12.972 --> 00:01:15.274
I don't have any money.
I don't have any money.

00:01:15.274 --> 00:01:16.376
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:01:16.376 --> 00:01:18.277
Hold the door, please.
Hold the door.

00:01:18.277 --> 00:01:19.545
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:01:19.545 --> 00:01:21.780
This is a two-bedroom?
Are you out of your mind?"

00:01:21.780 --> 00:01:23.983
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:01:23.983 --> 00:01:27.620
But make no mistake --
this is an improvisational city.

00:01:27.620 --> 00:01:30.356
I mean, you leave your house
and you're scatting, you know?

00:01:30.356 --> 00:01:32.859
[ Laughter ]
Subway's down, Uber's surging.

00:01:32.859 --> 00:01:33.760
I'm running.

00:01:33.760 --> 00:01:35.195
[ Laughter ]

00:01:35.195 --> 00:01:37.297
This is the only city you go,
"I guess I'm going to run."

00:01:37.297 --> 00:01:38.430
[ Laughter ]
I don't know.

00:01:38.430 --> 00:01:40.199
It's just another mode
of transportation.

00:01:40.199 --> 00:01:42.635
[ Laughter ]
People just run here, you know?

00:01:42.635 --> 00:01:43.502
And people get it.

00:01:43.502 --> 00:01:45.004
"What happened?"
I ran 40 blocks.

00:01:45.004 --> 00:01:47.306
People go, "Oh, I'm so sorry.
I had to run yesterday.

00:01:47.306 --> 00:01:48.374
Isn't it terrible?"

00:01:48.374 --> 00:01:50.409
[ Laughter ]

00:01:50.409 --> 00:01:54.814
I saw a guy running on the
George Washington Bridge

00:01:54.814 --> 00:01:57.650
and not an exercise guy...
[ Laughter ]

00:01:57.650 --> 00:02:00.320
...a suit guy, just running.

00:02:00.320 --> 00:02:01.420
[ Laughter ]

00:02:01.420 --> 00:02:04.923
If you see an exercise guy
on a bridge,

00:02:04.923 --> 00:02:06.459
you think,
"That guy is ambitious."

00:02:06.459 --> 00:02:08.828
But if you see
a suit guy running --

00:02:08.828 --> 00:02:12.431
just about anywhere,
but especially on a bridge --

00:02:12.431 --> 00:02:14.667
you think,
"That guy's in trouble."

00:02:14.667 --> 00:02:17.470
[ Laughter ]

00:02:17.470 --> 00:02:20.807
Where are you in your life that
you're in a suit and you go,

00:02:20.807 --> 00:02:22.407
"I'm on the wrong side
of the river!

00:02:22.407 --> 00:02:23.676
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:02:23.676 --> 00:02:25.077
Oh, no!

00:02:25.144 --> 00:02:26.379
Oh, no!

00:02:26.379 --> 00:02:27.846
Not again!"

00:02:27.846 --> 00:02:30.850
[ Cheering and applause ]

00:02:33.619 --> 00:02:35.420
I think that guy's dead.
I don't know.

00:02:35.420 --> 00:02:37.090
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:02:37.090 --> 00:02:42.128
I saw a guy on the subway
holding a Citi Bike

00:02:42.128 --> 00:02:44.497
and I can't stop thinking
about that guy.

00:02:44.497 --> 00:02:46.565
[ Laughter ]

00:02:46.565 --> 00:02:47.800
I was just looking at him like,

00:02:47.800 --> 00:02:49.034
"I don't know
where you're going,

00:02:49.034 --> 00:02:50.903
but I know there's a better way
to get there.

00:02:50.903 --> 00:02:51.804
I know."

00:02:51.804 --> 00:02:54.274
[ Laughter ]

00:02:54.274 --> 00:02:58.010
I mean, if you don't know,
Citi Bikes are these free bikes

00:02:58.010 --> 00:02:59.745
we have around the city
that you pay for.

00:02:59.745 --> 00:03:02.915
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:03:02.915 --> 00:03:04.750
You know them.

00:03:04.750 --> 00:03:07.720
He was on public transportation

00:03:07.720 --> 00:03:10.155
and holding
public transportation.

00:03:10.155 --> 00:03:11.657
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:03:11.657 --> 00:03:14.393
It was so perplexing, you know?

00:03:14.393 --> 00:03:16.562
What are you doing?
Did you pay twice?

00:03:16.562 --> 00:03:18.364
[ Laughter ]
I don't understand.

00:03:18.364 --> 00:03:20.133
It's very strange because we all

00:03:20.133 --> 00:03:21.800
make our travel plan
in the morning, you know?

00:03:21.800 --> 00:03:24.103
Like I'm going to take
this down and transfer there.

00:03:24.103 --> 00:03:25.438
And this guy had to be like...

00:03:25.438 --> 00:03:30.643
[ Laughter ]

00:03:30.643 --> 00:03:32.544
..."I'm overwhelmed.
I don't know.

00:03:32.544 --> 00:03:34.447
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:03:34.447 --> 00:03:36.882
I think I'm just going to pick
up the bike first, you know?

00:03:36.882 --> 00:03:38.517
[ Laughter ]
I don't want to be

00:03:38.517 --> 00:03:40.653
the only guy out there
without a bike, you know?

00:03:40.653 --> 00:03:43.623
[ Laughter ]
And then I'll just take it
down there with me.

00:03:43.623 --> 00:03:47.126
And once you get it down there,
you got to bring it back up.

00:03:47.126 --> 00:03:49.528
[ Laughter ]
And then maybe I can get an Uber

00:03:49.528 --> 00:03:51.831
and put it in the back of the
Uber, something like that.
[ Laughter ]

00:03:51.831 --> 00:03:53.098
I just want to get somewhere

00:03:53.098 --> 00:03:54.733
where I can ride this thing,
you know?

00:03:54.733 --> 00:03:56.903
[ Laughter ]
Been paying for it all day long.

00:03:56.903 --> 00:03:58.471
[ Laughter ]

00:03:59.972 --> 00:04:01.507
[ Laughter ]

00:04:01.507 --> 00:04:03.642
This is a tough city
to get around.

00:04:03.642 --> 00:04:05.911
You ever give someone directions
in New York City

00:04:05.911 --> 00:04:08.314
and then, two blocks later,
just go...

00:04:08.314 --> 00:04:11.717
[ Laughter ]

00:04:11.717 --> 00:04:14.353
..."Oh, no.
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:04:14.353 --> 00:04:16.188
I think I killed
that foreign family.

00:04:16.188 --> 00:04:17.457
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:04:17.457 --> 00:04:19.859
They are so dead
and there's nothing I can do."

00:04:19.859 --> 00:04:22.061
[ Laughter ]
I just want to call 911

00:04:22.061 --> 00:04:23.562
and be like, "I'm so sorry.

00:04:23.562 --> 00:04:25.397
There's this family

00:04:25.397 --> 00:04:27.567
and I sent them west
at Port Authority

00:04:27.567 --> 00:04:30.502
[ Laughter and applause ]
and all they wanted
was cheesecake

00:04:30.502 --> 00:04:32.638
and now, I can't sleep."

00:04:32.638 --> 00:04:36.342
[ Laughter ]

00:04:36.342 --> 00:04:38.644
My family's concerned
about me out here

00:04:38.644 --> 00:04:40.246
and they should be.

00:04:40.246 --> 00:04:42.114
[ Laughter ]
If you're a criminal

00:04:42.114 --> 00:04:43.449
and you see me walking around,

00:04:43.449 --> 00:04:45.651
your thought is,
"It's going to be a good day."

00:04:45.651 --> 00:04:48.454
[ Laughter ]
That's what you think.

00:04:48.454 --> 00:04:51.156
"I'm going to hit my quota early
and clock out, you know?"

00:04:51.156 --> 00:04:54.060
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:04:54.060 --> 00:04:55.495
Criminal half day.

00:04:55.495 --> 00:04:57.529
[ Laughter ]

00:04:57.529 --> 00:04:59.399
Like if I was ever on the phone

00:04:59.399 --> 00:05:00.666
with my father,
walking around the city,

00:05:00.666 --> 00:05:02.368
he'd always go,
"Son, where's your wallet?

00:05:02.368 --> 00:05:05.070
Put your wallet
in your front pocket."

00:05:05.070 --> 00:05:09.275
That was my dad's plan to foil
New York City's criminals.

00:05:09.275 --> 00:05:10.342
[ Laughter ]

00:05:10.342 --> 00:05:11.644
Just to switch my wallet

00:05:11.644 --> 00:05:14.079
over into the unexpected pocket
you know?

00:05:14.079 --> 00:05:16.549
[ Laughter ]
I don't know how this plays out,

00:05:16.549 --> 00:05:17.817
if you get held up, you know?

00:05:17.817 --> 00:05:19.518
it's like, "I hope
they don't come around.

00:05:19.518 --> 00:05:21.653
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:05:21.653 --> 00:05:23.789
I can't believe I'm getting
away with it right now.

00:05:23.789 --> 00:05:26.025
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:05:26.025 --> 00:05:27.826
My father's going
to be so proud."

00:05:27.826 --> 00:05:29.629
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:05:29.629 --> 00:05:31.230
"Where's the wallet, man?!
Where's the --"

00:05:31.230 --> 00:05:32.331
[ Snickers ]

00:05:32.331 --> 00:05:35.435
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:05:35.435 --> 00:05:36.335
I mean --

00:05:36.335 --> 00:05:38.071
[ Cheering ]

00:05:41.506 --> 00:05:44.043
This guy has no clue!

00:05:44.043 --> 00:05:46.245
What a rube, huh?
[ Laughter ]

00:05:46.245 --> 00:05:48.514
I guess he's never been
to Idaho before.

00:05:48.514 --> 00:05:49.815
[ Laughter, cheering,
and applause ]

00:05:49.815 --> 00:05:51.417
I'm Ryan Hamilton.

00:05:51.417 --> 00:05:52.451
Thank you very much.

00:05:52.451 --> 00:05:53.653
[ Whistling ]

00:05:55.487 --> 00:05:57.056
-Oh, my gosh!

00:05:57.056 --> 00:05:58.324
Thank you so much.

00:05:58.324 --> 00:06:00.192
[ Cheering, whistling,
and applause ]

00:06:00.192 --> 00:06:01.527
Ryan Hamilton!

00:06:01.527 --> 00:06:04.263
That's how you do it
right there.

00:06:04.263 --> 00:06:07.900
For more info,
go to ryanhamiltonlive.com.

00:06:07.900 --> 00:06:09.068
We'll be right back.

00:06:09.068 --> 00:06:11.037
Oh, my gosh!

